module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.trigger_satisfied_before_the_row_was_written

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data trigger_satisfied_before_the_row_was_written: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "trigger_satisfied_before_the_row_was_written" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a next-rung trigger naming a capability that had ALREADY SHIPPED when the row was written, so the class is born retired and its stall is permanent and invisible** (INVALID STATE: a class below its ceiling names a restoration or next-rung trigger, as section 4b(2) obliges it to, and the named capability was ALREADY PRESENT IN THE TREE AT FILING TIME. The trigger is therefore not a transition: there is no future event at which it becomes true, because it was never false. The row reads as tracked debt with a named exit and is in fact untracked -- nobody will retire it, because retiring it requires observing a change that already happened before anyone was watching. HARM: this is worse than an untriggered stall, because an untriggered stall at least presents as unfinished. A row with a satisfied trigger presents as COMPLETE WORK AWAITING AN EVENT, so it is skipped by exactly the audits that exist to find stalls, and the class it describes stays at its found rung indefinitely while the roster reports it as governed. THE GAP THAT ADMITS IT IS IN THE OBLIGATION ITSELF: section 4b(2) requires a class below ceiling to NAME its next-rung trigger and says nothing about that trigger being UNSATISFIED AT FILING TIME. Naming is checked by review and by the reader; satisfiability is checked by nobody.",

    "RECEIPT, AND IT IS THE STRONGEST KIND -- FOUND BY THE AUTHOR OF THE ROW WHILE WITHDRAWING IT, NOT BY AN AUDIT: session vivid-ibex-751 withdrew a finding of their own whose trigger read that the listing states its own truncation and total, against a capability that had shipped in gunbc#9648 a WEEK EARLIER. The trigger was true on the day it was written. Credit for the specimen is theirs and it is cited here as their withdrawal rather than as a third-party report, because the withdrawal is what makes it evidence: an author checking their own trigger against the tree is the only place this is currently caught.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, DECIDABLE AND CHEAP, WHICH IS WHY THIS IS A ROW AND NOT A NOTE: a trigger whose named capability PREDATES THE ROW'S OWN EARLIEST RECEIPT. Both operands are already carried -- the capability has a landing commit and the row has its receipts -- so the comparison needs no judgement and no new authority. A class whose detection needs judgement gets detected once.",

    "ITS EXACT DUAL IS ALREADY ROSTERED AS restoration_promise_names_a_route_that_does_not_exist, AND THE PAIR IS THE FINDING RATHER THAN EITHER HALF. That row is a trigger naming a run, lane, cadence or sweep the tree DOES NOT CONTAIN; this row is a trigger naming a capability the tree ALREADY CONTAINS. NOT-YET and ALREADY are TWO WAYS a named condition fails to be a TRANSITION, and both leave a class untracked while it reads as tracked. THIS IS DELIBERATELY NOT WRITTEN AS AN EXHAUSTIVE PAIR, and the reason is this row's own subject turned on itself: a closed count over a population nobody enumerated is the defect rostered as selection_view_read_as_population, and TWO IS THE NUMBER OF ARMS THE ROSTER HAPPENS TO HOLD TONIGHT, not a proof that a third is unwritable. At least one further arm is already conceivable -- a trigger whose satisfaction is UNDECIDABLE, which is neither not-yet nor already and cannot fire for a third reason -- and it is unrostered because nobody has hit it, which is exactly the evidence a closed claim would have suppressed. The axis is offered as a DISCOVERED PAIR to search along, never as a partition to check membership against -- the first as a promise that can never fire, the second as tracking that fired before anyone was watching.",

    "WHY TWO ROWS AND NOT ONE ROW WITH TWO ARMS, STATED EXPLICITLY BECAUSE A READER LANDING ON THE PAIR WILL ASK AND AN UNSTATED ANSWER READS AS AN OVERSIGHT. The test applied is whether the REPAIRS diverge, and they do, in both the detection and the remedy. DETECTION: the dual is decided against THE TREE'S CONTENTS -- does the named route exist -- and is at ceiling 3 for exactly that reason; this row is decided against THE ROW'S OWN RECEIPT DATES, which the tree does not need to be consulted for at all. REMEDY: the dual is repaired by BUILDING THE ROUTE the trigger names, or by rescoping the promise to one that exists -- work outside the row. This row is repaired by RE-TRIAGING THE CLASS ITSELF, because a trigger that was already true means the class's current rung was never re-measured after the capability landed, so the row may be at ceiling already, may have climbed silently, or may be genuinely stalled for a different reason nobody has looked for -- work inside the row. Different evidence, different actor, different artifact touched. They are cited to each other rather than merged.",

    "THREE NEARBY ROWS THAT ARE NOT THIS ONE, RECORDED BECAUSE THE THIRD WILL BE RE-LITIGATED. self_authorized_dissolution is about a trigger offered as PERMISSION to create debt rather than as a lifecycle fact -- an authority question, not a satisfiability one, and a trigger can be validly authorized and still satisfied at birth. a_written_row_is_not_a_firing_mechanism is about a row STANDING IN FOR a mechanism -- and a trigger satisfied at birth may sit under a perfectly real, perfectly firing mechanism, which is what makes it invisible. predicate_vacuously_true_on_an_empty_domain is the closest in flavour and still a different subject: its domain is empty at EVALUATION time and its harm is a verdict read as evidence, whereas this is satisfied at FILING time and its harm is a transition that can never occur.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, and the mitigation is that an author happens to check their own trigger against the tree while withdrawing something else. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- a trigger carrying the capability it names, rather than prose describing it, admits a filing-time comparison against that capability's landing, so no Accepted program can file a row whose trigger is already discharged. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a CAPABILITY and not an artifact, and stated so it cannot itself be satisfied at birth: the trigger field is typed as a reference to the capability it names rather than as prose, AND the roster refuses a row whose referenced capability predates the row's own earliest receipt. Neither half alone is sufficient -- the typed reference without the refusal is a shape that permits the state, and the refusal without the typed reference has no operand to compare.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
